  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Image\'s Visuals**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the uploaded image, `original-5aa8c6c24e0b084c1079cfc7727ca927.webp`, to assess its visual aesthetic. The initial observation is the background, which appears clean. I\'ll need to identify the other components and their interrelation.\n\n\n**Observing the Interface Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the interface components. I see a modern, airy slate-gray background, almost `#EEF2F6`. The crisp white cards, `#FFFFFF`, have rounded edges and a soft shadow, very clean. The top navigation bar features a blue logo, \"DochGames,\" and a pill-style menu with an active vibrant lime-yellow \"Dashboard\" tab. On the right, search, notification, settings, and user avatar icons are present. I\'m moving on to dissecting the metric stack now.\n\n\n**Dissecting Key Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the statistical elements. The design features light-blue and light-red rounded square icon containers. The \"Followers\" stat has a user icon, showing \"128,420\" with a \"\342\206\221 25%\" green badge. Then, there\'s \"Likes\" showing \"66,816\" and \"\342\206\221 32%\". The second card displays the \"Click-through rate (CTR)\" and a bar chart, showing stacked bars with a light grayish/soft blue-gray background with orange / tangerine bars.\n\n\n**Examining the Chart Visuals**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down card three\'s \"Audience Growth\" visualization. It\'s a smooth, curved blue line chart with a gradient fill, with a tooltip. I\'m noting the year, week, and day toggles. I see a black pill tooltip at the peak, showing a dashed vertical indicator and the X and Y axis labels, but need to examine how the line interacts with the labels.\n\n**Mapping Audience Locations**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the fourth card. This one maps \"Audience Location.\" It\'s a world map visualization in an SVG format, and I see vibrant royal and periwinkle blue highlights, along with an \"Export Report\" button. I\'m focusing on how the countries are highlighted and how the different color hues are interacting.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Final Cards**\n\nI\'m now examining the remaining visual elements. Card five presents a \"Sentiment Analysis\" with a radial gauge, red to green, displaying a score of `4.85` and a \"Positive\" badge. Finally, card six highlights \"Total Customers\" at `2,420` with a growth indicator and a user avatar preview, offering a \"Show All\" link at the end.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 237602108
    }
