  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Reference Image**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the reference image. The clean, light background using crisp modern SaaS style colors (`#F1F5F9` or `#F3F6FA`) is the first thing to note. Furthermore, I see white rounded cards with gentle borders (like `border border-slate-200/80` or `border border-slate`).\n\n\n**Observing the Navigation Bar**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the navigation bar. The DochGames brand mark, featuring a geometric logo in royal blue, is prominent. I\'ve noted the segmented tabs in the middle: the bright lime/chartreuse pill button for \"Dashboard,\" and other options like \"Content,\" \"Finance,\" and \"Reports,\" which might also be labeled as \"Widgets,\" \"Monetization,\" or \"Analytics.\" On the right, there\'s the usual search, notifications, settings, and user profile with dropdown.\n\n\n**Examining the Charts**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the charts. Card B shows a key metric, the Click-Through Rate, with a bar chart visualizing monthly performance. The bright orange bars against the light gray background are eye-catching. Then, Card C presents a growth curve for audience engagement, using a sleek sine-wave. The blue line and interactive tooltip for the \"This Year\" view are clear.\n\n\n**Detailing the Regional Data**\n\nI\'m now detailing regional data visualization. I\'ve got color-coding for countries mapped out: #60A5FA for US/Canada, #93C5FD for Ukraine/Europe, and a light gray for Australia and the rest. The right panel will showcase \"Top Countries\" with flags, names, and animated progress bars showing percentages.\n\n**Reviewing the Gauge and Metrics**\n\nThe new card E includes a sentiment analysis gauge, a speedometer with a red-to-green gradient. I\'m noting the happy/sad emoji, the score, and the positive badge. Card F will display total customers, an increasing trend, overlapping avatars, and a link to view all.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Principles**\n\nI\'m now establishing the core UI principles. This rebuild needs a high-clarity SaaS aesthetic using light, airy backgrounds (`#F4F6F9`), crisp white cards with rounded edges, and clean sans-serif typography. I\'m focusing on color accents: Royal Blue (`#2563EB`) as primary, Lime/Chartreuse (`#D4F826`) for active highlights, Tangerine/Orange (`#FF6B2C`) for data, and Emerald Green (`#16A34A`) for growth indicators.\n\n\n**Defining the Visual Components**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the visual components. I see a need for soft slate grays to balance things out. I\'m focusing on the navigation bar, now, to accurately match the image\'s top bar styling, from logo to right-hand icons. I\'m starting to build out a role selector. I am noting the importance of the dashboard cards for the Publisher and Developer views. I\'m already envisioning the double stat metric card.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Features and Functionality**\n\nI\'ve outlined every existing feature, ensuring preservation. I\'m focusing on the Role Switcher and its corresponding views. Publisher features, like the \"Connect Property\" modal and \"Widget Builder,\" are being prioritized to ensure a smooth transition. The focus is on aligning the rebuild with the initial requirements. I\'ve noted the need to maintain all features while updating the design.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 516612380
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
