  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the visual elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the image\'s components. I\'ve broken down the top bar: a stylized blue icon with four rounded lobes, followed by the brand name \"TrendTide\" or \"DochGames.\" I\'m looking for the perfect logo mark. It features a segmented pill container with a light-gray background in the center.\n\n\n**Examining key dashboard elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the suggested dashboard cards. My goal is to determine the ideal display of followers and likes in the metric stack layout. I\'m focusing on visual cues like the rounded corners, padding, and subtle shadow for the \"Followers & Likes\" card. The card will feature a crisp white background. I\'m also considering the ideal layout for metrics, like user icons, a subtitle, a value and growth badge inline.\n\n\n**Refining Card Metrics**\n\nI\'m now refining the metric display within the cards. For the bottom metric, I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy: a light rose heart icon, a subtle \"Likes\" subtitle, a bold value of \"66,816,\" and a growth badge of \"\342\206\221 32%.\" I\'m prioritizing optimal readability and visual appeal to convey the data effectively.\n\n\n**Visualizing data trends**\n\nI\'m now sketching out the line chart to display the trend data. I\'m visualizing the X-axis labels: Jan through Aug and the Y-axis labels: 80k, 60k, 40k, and 20k. I\'m focusing on a smooth SVG spline curve in rich blue with a soft vertical gradient fill. I want an interactive tooltip at the peak in March, and I\'m designing a dark, rounded tooltip bubble with a triangle pointer and dashed line.\n\n**Designing geographical card**\n\nNext, I\'m working on the bottom row of cards. I have the rough layout now, with the Audience Location card spanning about 65% of the width. I\'m visualizing a \"Audience Location\" header with an \"Export Report \342\206\223\" button. I\'m now working on the left side of the card, a world map SVG with continents in a soft gray, with the United States and Canada highlighted in a vibrant royal blue.\n\n\n**Mapping the world data**\n\nNow, I\'m defining the geographical visualization. I\'ve colored Western and Eastern Europe (Ukraine, Spain, UK, France) in royal blue, and Australia in periwinkle. Interactive hover tooltips will show traffic and player count. On the right, \"Top Countries\" will be displayed: USA with a progress bar, followed by Canada, Ukraine, Spain, and the UK.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Structuring card relationships**\n\nI am now focusing on the bottom-right column\'s stacked cards. The top card will provide a Sentiment Analysis, featuring a radial gauge from red to green, emojis, and a score with a \"Positive\" badge. Underneath this will be a \"Total Customers\" card with a number, growth, and avatar row.\n\n\n**Organizing interactive elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating interactive elements into the dashboard, specifically focusing on a \"Show All\" link to reveal partner studios or a syndication breakdown. Below the executive grid, I\'m incorporating interactive game distribution tools. This includes a Live Widget Tester for previewing game formats, quick launch widget formats, a property key generator, and real-time notification updates.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 530556205
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
